+# PROPOSED — NOT IN FORCE — AWAITS THE FOUNDER'S RULING
+
+Joint round `asking_predicate_and_fourth_standard_2026-11-14`. This file is
+INERT by construction: `bench/cdsfl_registry/composer.py` reads the universal
+directive by exact filename (`cdsfl_core_formal.md` / `cdsfl_core.txt`, lines
+356-357 and 799-800) and never globs this directory, verified by reading the
+collection code this round. Seat cc2's blind finding stands: text placed in
+`cdsfl_core_formal.md` itself becomes HARD on every seat the moment it
+contains MUST/NEVER/"inadmissible", because `_block_is_hard()` is pure marker
+containment with no ratification notion. Do not move this text there before
+ruling on it.
+
+PROVENANCE. One merged text from 2 blind proposals: placement as a scope
+correction (seat cc2); the ordinal consequence ordering and the runnable-
+invariant clause (seat fable); the consumer-enumeration and invisible-
+direction step (seat cc2). Each clause blocks a failure measured in this
+project's record, cited inline.
+
+---
+
+**HIL-consequence (a scope correction to SIMPLEST SUFFICIENT — not a 4th
+competing criterion).** "Sufficient" includes consequence to the human in the
+loop: where a change alters anything he reads and acts on — a count, a list, a
+named next step, a verdict, a budget — the fix has not discharged the
+requirement until that consequence is accounted for, so no precedence rule
+between standards is created or needed. Consequence is classified on the HIL
+surface's own ordinal scale, whose ordering is: silent omission of something
+he must act on, above visible over-report, above cosmetic cost, with the
+critical level at silent omission; it is reported on the surface's own terms
+(the figure, the list, the stalled entry), never as a bare number, because the
+declared `software` scale (CVSS v4.0 base score, `domain_manifest.toml`)
+presupposes an attacker and cannot score a defect that has none. A proposed
+fix must enumerate EVERY consumer of the changed value, by file and line, and
+state for each the direction in which an error there is invisible to him; a
+fix with an unenumerated consumer or an unnamed invisible direction is
+inadmissible, and a fix that moves any error toward silent omission is a
+regression regardless of its aggregate accuracy (measured instance: the same
+OWED verdict that over-counts on the `[tasks]` banner silently removes entries
+at `work_not_narrate._first_movable`, this round, executed falsifier).
+Symmetrically with the additive standard, every application of this clause
+ships a runnable invariant for the direction it claims safe — or states
+plainly that none can be written — else it is the next addition nothing
+reaches (11 such measured since 2026-08-01). Where the change touches no
+surface the HIL reads, the clause is silent.

